From: hoangvu12 <hggaming91@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 05:03:38 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Images from another device load in a few round trips, not one
 per chunk

Over the relay each chunk read is a round trip (~100 ms between two
networks), and the app read a remote image's 45 KB chunks one after
another: a 1 MB image waited 23 times in a row.

- engine: ReadAttachmentChunk and ReadChatImageChunk replies carry the
  file's `size`.
- ui/attachments.rs: after the first chunk, the rest are asked for 8 at a
  time and joined in order. With a size, exactly the chunks the file has;
  from an older engine without one, reads run ahead to the chunk that says
  `done` (at most a window past the end). A later chunk that fails is
  retried twice, so a relay link dropping mid-image costs a retry, not the
  image. A chunk that doesn't line up fails the image rather than tearing
  it.

Nothing changes on the relay or the edge.

Tests: ui chunks_are_read_several_at_a_time_and_retried_when_dropped,
ui attachments (36), reply_image (2), transcript (136/137; the one
failure, expanded_tool_call_text_drag_selects, passes alone 3/3), engine
reply_images (4), uploads:: (15), chat_image (1), e2e image tests (2),
device_routing relayed image size (the test's later terminal step still
times out on Windows, as before).
